message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on an artificial pear decoration. Artificial fruit of plastic generally falls under heading 6702, "Artificial flowers, foliage and fruit and parts thereof; articles made of artificial flowers, foliage or fruit." Subheading 6702.10 covers plastic articles, with 6702.10.20 for "Other" plastic items and 6702.10.40 for other. The 6702.10 subheadings are: 6702.10.20 "Christmas ornaments" and 6702.10.40 "Other". There is also a 6702.90 group for other materials.

The pear is made of polyresin plastic with an iron stem, and it is not a Christmas ornament. Even so, the artificial fruit of heading 6702 could be classified as plastic, since the plastic body gives the essential character. The statistical suffix for 6702.10.40 is 6702.10.4000.

{"hts_code": "6702.10.4000", "reason": "Artificial pear of flocked polyresin plastic with an iron stem is artificial fruit of plastics (not a Christmas ornament) under heading 6702, subheading 6702.10.40."}
